IO-26: convert wind speed from a user-prepared climate file to mph

parseUserFileLine() stored the wind speed column as read. SWMM works in mph
internally, and the manual says a user-prepared climate file gives wind speed
in km/hour for metric units, as the WINDSPEED MONTHLY values are (which
setWind() divides by UCF(WINDSPEED)). In SI models the file's wind speed was
used 1.608 times too large in rain-on-snow melt and reported 1.608 times too
large by swmm_getValue(swmm_WINDSPEED). Divide by UCF(WINDSPEED) when the
value is read. US models (factor 1) are unchanged.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply IO-26_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/climate.c b/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
index c343b93..50079ba 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/climate.c
@@ -1604,9 +1604,9 @@ void parseUserFileLine()
     if (strlen(s2) > 0 && *s2 != '*')
         FileData[EVAP][d] = atof(s2);
 
-    // --- process WIND
+    // --- process WIND (km/hr for SI units ==> mph)
     if (strlen(s3) > 0 && *s3 != '*')
-        FileData[WIND][d] = atof(s3);
+        FileData[WIND][d] = atof(s3) / UCF(WINDSPEED);
 }
 
 /*!
